%description:
A mobile node away from home reverse-tunnels its traffic through its home agent, which
decapsulates each datagram and forwards the inner one toward the correspondent node.

This is a regression test for the arrival interface of a decapsulated datagram. RFC 4861
Section 8.2 lets a router send a Redirect only when, among other conditions, "the Source
Address field of the packet identifies a neighbor". A reverse-tunneled datagram does not
arrive on a link at all -- it arrives through the tunnel, which RFC 2473 Section 3 models
as a link of its own -- and its source, the mobile node's home address, is not a neighbor
on the physical interface the outer datagram came in on. The inner datagram used to keep
that physical interface, so the home agent, forwarding it back out of the same interface,
believed it was redirecting an on-link neighbor and sent a Redirect to a node that was not
on the link. Because Ipv6.ned defaults sendRedirects to true, a home agent did this without
any configuration whenever it forwarded reverse-tunneled traffic back out of its arrival
interface.

This configuration leaves sendRedirects at its default, so the home agent would send those
Redirects if the defect were reintroduced. The test asserts that it sends none, and -- so
that the assertion cannot pass merely because no datagram was ever reverse-tunneled -- that
the home agent really does decapsulate tunneled traffic during the run.

The Redirect check also passes when the Redirect is suppressed for another reason, such as
a check that the source is a neighbor. The test therefore also asserts the arrival interface
itself: the home agent routes the decapsulated datagram as arriving on its tunnel interface
(ip6tun...), not on the physical interface.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
**.mipv6.cmdenv-log-level = trace
**.ipv6.ipv6.cmdenv-log-level = trace
**.ipv6.neighbourDiscovery.cmdenv-log-level = trace
**.app[*].cmdenv-log-level = trace
**.cmdenv-log-level = off
cmdenv-event-banners = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
network = inet.test.moduletest.lib.Mipv6RoamingNetwork
sim-time-limit = 40s
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = "%C: "
num-rngs = 3
seed-set = 1
**.mobility.rng-0 = 2

*.total_mn = 1
*.total_cn = 1

**.neighbourDiscovery.minIntervalBetweenRAs = 0.03s
**.neighbourDiscovery.maxIntervalBetweenRAs = 0.07s
**.neighbourDiscovery.detectL2Movement = false

*.radioMedium.mediumLimitCache.maxTransmissionPower = 2.0mW
*.radioMedium.mediumLimitCache.minReceptionPower = -82dBm
*.radioMedium.mediumLimitCache.minInterferencePower = -82dBm

**.wlan*.mgmt.numAuthSteps = 4
**.AP*.wlan*.mgmt.beaconInterval = 0.1s
**.AP_Home.wlan*.mgmt.ssid = "HOME"
**.AP_Home.wlan*.address = "10:AA:00:00:00:01"
**.AP_Home.eth[0].address = "10:AE:00:00:00:02"
**.AP_Home.eth[0].duplexMode = true
**.AP_1.wlan*.mgmt.ssid = "AP1"
**.AP_1.wlan*.address = "10:AA:00:00:A1:01"
**.AP_1.eth[0].address = "10:AE:00:00:A1:02"
**.AP_1.eth[0].duplexMode = true
**.AP_2.wlan*.mgmt.ssid = "AP2"
**.AP_2.wlan*.address = "10:AA:00:00:A2:01"
**.AP_2.eth[0].address = "10:AE:00:00:A2:02"
**.AP_2.eth[0].duplexMode = true

**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 0m
**.MN[0].mobility.typename = "RectangleMobility"
**.MN[0].mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 180m
**.MN[0].mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 170m
**.MN[0].mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 950m
**.MN[0].mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 180m
**.MN[0].mobility.startPos = 0
**.MN[0].mobility.speed = 10mps
**.MN*.mobility.updateInterval = 0.1s

# CN pings the MN's home address throughout; the replies must follow the MN across both handovers
**.MN*.numApps = 0
**.CN*.numApps = 1
**.CN*.app[*].typename = "PingApp"
**.CN[0].app[0].destAddr = "aaaa:0:66:0:8aa:ff:fe00:b"
**.CN*.app[0].packetSize = 56B
**.CN*.app[0].sendInterval = 0.5s
**.CN[0].app[0].startTime = 1s
**.CN*.app[0].hopLimit = 32
**.CN*.app[0].printPing = true

**.forwarding = false
**.eth[*].queue.typename = "EthernetQosQueue"
**.eth[*].queue.dataQueue.typename = "DropTailQueue"
**.eth[*].queue.dataQueue.packetCapacity = 10
**.eth*.duplexMode = true
**.analogModel.ignorePartialInterference = true
**.AP_Home.wlan*.radio.channelNumber = 1
**.AP_1.wlan*.radio.channelNumber = 2
**.AP_2.wlan*.radio.channelNumber = 3
**.MN*.wlan*.radio.channelNumber = 0
**.wlan*.agent.activeScan = true
**.wlan*.agent.defaultSsid = ""
**.wlan*.agent.channelsToScan = "1 2 3"
**.wlan*.agent.probeDelay = 0.1s
**.wlan*.agent.minChannelTime = 0.15s
**.wlan*.agent.maxChannelTime = 0.3s
**.wlan*.agent.authenticationTimeout = 5s
**.wlan*.agent.associationTimeout = 5s
**.wlan*.bitrate = 2Mbps
**.wlan*.mac.dcf.channelAccess.cwMin = 7
**.radio.transmitter.power = 2.0mW
**.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.constraintAreaMaxX = 1050m
**.constraintAreaMaxY = 850m

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%subst: /omnetpp:://
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%# the home agent really does decapsulate reverse-tunneled traffic in this run
%contains: stdout
Mipv6RoamingNetwork.Home_Agent.ipv6.ipv6: Tunnelled IP datagram
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%# the decapsulated datagram is routed as arriving on the tunnel interface
%contains: stdout
Mipv6RoamingNetwork.Home_Agent.ipv6.ipv6: Routing the decapsulated datagram as arriving on ip6tun
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%# the defect itself: forwarding a decapsulated datagram must not trigger a Redirect
%not-contains: stdout
Mipv6RoamingNetwork.Home_Agent.ipv6.neighbourDiscovery: Sending ICMPv6 Redirect
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
